  "text": "Whereas, the National Association of Women Business Owners, NABO, of Greater DC, was founded in 1975 as the inaugural chapter of NABO, launching a national movement dedicated to supporting and advocating for women entrepreneurs. And whereas, for five decades, NABO Greater DC has been a powerful force for advocacy, education, mentorship, and networking, empowering women entrepreneurs across Maryland, Washington DC, and Northern Virginia to start, grow, and scale their businesses. And whereas, NABO has played a critical role in shaping public policy and advancing economic opportunities for women business owners, including its advocacy for the Women's Business Ownership Act of 1988, HR 5050, which eliminated discriminatory lending practices and established key federal resources for women-owned businesses. And whereas, NABO Greater DC continues to be a leader in economic development and entrepreneurship, contributing to the growth of Virginia's small business community and fostering a more inclusive and prosperous business environment for all. And whereas, NABO Greater DC will commemorate this milestone 50th anniversary at the NABO DC Women of Excellence Gala on March 14, 2025, at Sequoia DC, and NABO National will further recognize this achievement at the NABO Women's Business Conference from June 5 to 8, 2025, at the Omni Shorm in Washington DC. And whereas, it is fitting that the City of Fairfax recognize NABO's Greater DC's half-century of leadership, impact, and unwavering commitment to advancing women in business."
